{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/946975-porting-vtm-to-vtr","id":946975,"title":"Porting VtM to VtR","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-09T08:55:53-07:00","id":946975,"title":"Porting VtM to VtR","content":"Been working on adapting, wanted to get input. I've seen the Translation Guide, but I was thinking more along these lines:<br /> <br /> Camarilla- a Covenant that is a blend of the Invictus and Carthian merits<br /> Sabbat- a Covenant that is a blend of the Ordo and Belials Brood<br /> Inconnu- Mystery Cult?<br /> <br /> Assamites- Covenant with Merges Sorcery<br /> Brujah- what Sabbat Daeva call themselves<br /> Cappadocians/Giovanni- Mystery Cult<br /> Daeva- Camarilla Clan<br /> Followers of Set- Mystery Cult<br /> Gangrel- Camarilla Clan<br /> Lasombra- Sabbat Ventrue<br /> Malkavians- Sabbat Mekhet<br /> Mekhet- Camarilla Clan<br /> Nosferatu- Camarilla Clan<br /> Niktuku- Sabbat Nosferatu<br /> Ravnos- Sabbat Gangrel<br /> Ventrue- Camarilla Clan<br /> <br /> Toreador- major Camarilla bloodline, Daeva/Ventrue<br /> Tzimisce- major Sabbat bloodline, Gangrel/Ventrue<br /> Tremere- sub-Covenant of Camarilla, Theban Sorcery<br /> Koldun- sub-Covenant of Sabbat, Cruac<br /> <br /> Black Hand- Mystery Cult<br /> Tal'Mahe'Ra- Mystery Cult<br /> Baali- Ahranite Sorcery option from VII, but with Wells of Sacrifice instead of the cauldron<br /> <br /> I've worked out some of the Mystery Cult stuff, but would love to get suggestions from anyone that may have done their own versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T12:35:53-07:00","id":947163,"title":"","content":"I think about this a lot, albeit less about <i>Masquerade'</i>s sects. I largely tie to the fall the of the (VtR) Camarilla and the creation of Invictus.<br /> <br /> Brujah - Successors of a long dead, but not forgotten Carthaginian covenant. Until some time in the Dark Ages, they continued to follow the teachings of Tanitbaal-Sahar, a philosophy that rejected authority and restraint. This put them at odds with Invictus and the Lancea et Sanctum. Modern Brujah are usually Carthians, but their anarchist tendencies are often better received within the Circle of the Crone.<br /> <br /> Malkavians - In VtR, it's possible to record memories in vitae. Malkavians are the result of a cabal of Mekhet seers in antiquity sharing blood containing a vast Lovecraftian knowledge, allegedly either from each other or a single legendary elder. It was so effective that it persists from sire to childe, but it drives them insane and none of them can recall more than fragments.<br /> <br /> Toreador - Think Rafael de Corazon, but for Invictus. The fall of the Camarilla was a tragedy for them and they helped to create Invictus to bring their way of life back. Mostly Daeva, with some Mekhet.<br /> <br /> Tremere - Either Mekhet or an artificial clan that use a reconstructed form of Veneficia (Veneficia was a Roman form of blood sorcery that invoked the power of the gods, but didn't require faith at all. Just meticulous rituals). They operate within Invictus.<br /> <br /> Ventrue - Descendants of the other side of Invictus i.e. barbarian warlords who embraced a new (to them) form of vampiric civilisation.<br /> <br /> Lasombra - The emerging leaders of the Lancea et Sanctum. A Persian legacy of either Daeva or Ventrue. The implication is that have been in the lower echelons of Roman kindred society they they joined a subversive cult (see above) and used it to destroy the Camarilla and set up a new power base around the Mediterranean.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce - Mostly Gangrel from land without Ventrue or similar clans. They traditionally rely upon ghouling, animalism, terror and a form of blood sorcery like Cruac, to dominate man, beast and land. Historically, they existed outside both the Camarilla and Invictus, although many of those in the Eastern Roman Empire joined the Lancea et Sanctum. The Ordo Dracul developed within their culture.<br /> <br /> Assamite - A small covenant based in Alamut. Mostly Mekhet. Distrusted (and rightly so), but useful.<br /> <br /> Cappadocians - An extinct covenant similar to the Ordo Dracul, albeit reverent to God in a strange way.<br /> <br /> Lamia - A cult much like the Circle of the Crone in some of its beliefs and practices that existed in a symbiotic relationship with the Cappadocians.<br /> <br /> Giovanni - A Ventrue former Cappadocian line that betrayed the covenant and formed an insular bloc within Invictus.<br /> <br /> Setites - A neo-Kemetic covenant that formed in opposition to the Lancea et Sanctum. Like the Circle of the Crone, but older as an institution and with different philosophies.<br /> <br /> Salubri - A legacy of Ventrue who try to resist their Beasts and use their vampiric abilities to help others. Most of them truly are well meaning, largely because of what type of person is chosen for a Salubri embrace. However, attempting using their own vitae to heal the body and dominate to heal the soul tends to cause complications, holds them back from achieving humanity to fullest and earns distrust from other kindred to say the least.<br /> <br /> Ravnos - I don't know. Something with nightmare. Unrelated to any of the big five covenants.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:20:31-07:00","id":947192,"title":"","content":"Interesting post. I'd start by asking why you want to translate VtM into VtR in the first place: is it a theoretical exercise or do you plan to play it? Depending on your goals and type of story you want to build, many different approaches are possible. <br /> <br /> While preparing a similar adaptation a few years back, my goal was to run a Gehenna-prophecies heavy chronicle focused on the Tremere using VtR rules. In such a concept, it was impossible to discard the VtM clans system for the VtR bloodline-heavy approach: the lore was just so intertwined with the 13 antediluvians and their presence permeating across the centuries that we'd need to rewrite the cosmology. I finally decided to keep all the VtM lore intact, 13 clans, the VtM clan disciplines (adapted to the VtR rules), and even generation instead of Blood Potency. The rest of the game system was VtR, which the group unanimously considered superior in almost all aspects. It worked great for us, as it kept the feeling and flavor of VtM intact, while enjoying a superior game system that got far less in the way of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1745-nox-ascensa","name":"Nox Ascensa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T15:29:15-07:00","id":947261,"title":"","content":"It's pretty much a mental exercise. Haven't played in years, but was with VtM back in first edition. When VtR came out, not only did I love the system, but it also brought me back to how VtM felt back in the day. I figured I could exercise a creative muscle by playing Golden Rule with it all.<br /> <br /> I figure, go with the rule system for VtR, bring over the Sects, and convert extra Clans into, well, what I posted above.<br /> <br /> Rather than focusing on Antediluvians, Gehenna, and metaplot heavy, it could be a setting more like VtR. I envision the Camarilla as basically the vampires that try to embrace the Man. The Sabbat embrace the Beast. They clash at times, but it's not like VtM where there is outright war.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla focus on tradition, deferring to Elders, maintaining the Masquerade. The Sabbat focus on what it means to be a monster, paying lip service to an idea (primarily pushed by the cult of the Black Hand) that there are ancient vampires, possibly even Clan founders, that manipulate it all and will want to consume younger vampires.<br /> <br /> I envision the TalMaheRa as the flip side of the Black Hand. They want to serve these ancients. Which group came first? Did the other group form as opposition to that? Up to Storyteller.<br /> <br /> The Inconnu is a cult, maybe Covenant, mostly Elders, that decided they tired of night to night politicking among the Kindred and just want to be left alone. The few who've heard of them talk all kinds of crazy, like they monitor cities, pit Sabbat against Camarilla, are all on Golconda...<br /> <br /> The Assamites are an old Covenant that believe in watching and punishing the excess of the Kindred; Giovanni are a group of Kindred that took over a death cult; Setites are also a cult centered around liberation through corruption.<br /> <br /> While there are all kinds of bloodlines, I wanted to make two major ones (one each Camarilla and Sabbat), both being dual Clan, and both being tied to Ventrue (whom weren't around in Ancient Rome, so it can make for interesting stories as to why the Julii are extinct and both major Covenants have these bloodlines).<br /> <br /> I figured Theban Sorcery is more about will to power, less about Gd. Cruac is more about the power of your blood, so tied more to the Beast and less to goddess.<br /> <br /> Finally, I've absolutely loved the Baali since the clanbook, and figured to keep them. Just need to figure out what would port over best. I definitely like the idea of using Shadad from VII, and making it a Well of Sacrifice instead.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the input folks, if I think of more ill post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:07:55-07:00","id":947370,"title":"","content":"There's a published VtM to VtR conversion book, iirc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:12:07-07:00","id":947681,"title":"","content":"Ehhh... I think you're making it too complicated.<br /> Invictus = Camarilla. Carthians = Anarchs. Inconnu = Ordo Dracul Sworn of the Ladder*, Sabbat = Lancea Sanctum + Circle of the Crone (Path of Lilith/Typhoon/etc). Subgroups like the Black Hand are nothing more than military factions of the major groups - that doesn't need anything new.<br /> <br /> The different clans (and bloodlines like Kiasyd) would just be VtR bloodlines with appropriate powers. Everyone starts in an appropriate bloodline.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, remaking things from either game into the other is actually simple. The problem comes from setting details that don't quite work rather than clans or factions. For instance, Blood Potency versus Generation. The Caine mythos and Antideluvians versus the strix. Differences between disciplines (especially how Nightmare basically ate parts of Presence and Chimerstry). What Humanity measures in each game. Those are the things that are hard to port over.<br /> <br /> <br /> * This is true - the Ladder is based on the Inconnu; in fact, the Ordo Dracul is basically all different forms of Golconda, both good and horrific, mixed together and given a new name. Tzim evolution, turning human (yes, I'm aware its a heresy in VtR, but heresies mean that its an actual on going issue), Tremere wanting their vampy-ascension, etc. All there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-10-2016, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:44:41-07:00","id":949625,"title":"","content":"But if I didn't make it complicated, it wouldn't be much of a mental exercise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. On a serious note, you gave me the idea of keeping VtR as is, but making a couple Mystery Cults to represent what I like about the Black Hand, Tal'Mahe'Ra, Giovanni/Cappadocians, and Setites. I still want a Baali Covenant with a Wells of Sacrifice though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:59:01-07:00","id":949790,"title":"","content":"I wrote these up as part of a bigger document a billion years ago, and I still haven't completed it, but this all might be useful to you.<br /> <br /> <b>Camarilla: </b><b>The Ivory Tower</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage:</b> The Camarilla not only controls the Masquerade, it masters it. Any time a Camarilla character reaches a breaking point in service of the Masquerade, she adds her Camarilla Status to the detachment roll, and gains an additional Beat. If the breaking point occurs during a sanctioned blood hunt, this bonus is doubled, even for diablerie. Because the Masquerade cannot be maintained in a vacuum, Camarilla members also gain a number of Contacts and Allies equal to their Status, distributed as the player likes.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> All Invictus<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat: </b><b>The Sword of Cain</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage:</b> Members of the Sabbat may purchase <b>Sabbat</b> <b>Ritae</b>, blood rituals that allow the Sabbat to maintain and reward loyalty. Mechanically, these are the same as <b>Invictus Blood Oaths</b>. Unlike Blood Oaths, however, Sabbat may only share Ritae with characters they have participated in a Vaulderie with.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Anointed, The Mother Daughter Bond, Riding the Wave<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Anarchs: </b><b>The Revolution</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage:</b> Members of the Anarch Movement may purchase <b>Anarch Law</b>, a set of occult regulations that maintain their independence from the Camarilla. Mechanically, this is the same as <b>Carthian Law</b>, albeit with the limitation that Anarch Law only functions in established Anarch domains.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>All Carthian.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra: The Black Hand</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage:</b> Members of the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra may purchase their own version of the Mystery Cult Initiation Merit in lieu of Status (below). In addition, for each dot of Initiation, the character may distribute a number of dots in Retainer and Allies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>House Tremere: </b><b>The Eye of the Pyramid</b><br /> <br /> <b>Advantage: </b>Tremere may purchase <b>Thaumaturgy</b>. Mechanically, this Discipline is the same as <b>Theban Sorcery</b>. However, the dice pool for Thaumaturgy is <b>Intelligence + Occult + Thaumaturgy</b>. As a sub-faction of the Camarilla, members of the Pyramid with Status in its ranks benefit from its Advantage, though they may not purchase its Merits without Storyteller permission, as their organization is often far removed from the rank and file of the Ivory Tower.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Lorekeeper, Sworn<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra Initiation (</b><b>\u2022 \u2013 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 </b>Gain the Specialty \u201cNoddist Lore\u201d in Academics.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 </b>Gain Language (Enochian)<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 </b>Gain two dots in the Unnatural Affinity Merit for ghosts and mages.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 </b>Gain the Omen Sensitivity Merit.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> Gain access to a 5 dot Haven in the lost city of Enoch, hidden in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat Ritae</b><br /> <br /> <b>Priest (</b><b>\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Sabbat Status \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Use <b>Notary </b>(<b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>, p. 117). It has the same effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Vaulderie (</b><b>\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> This ritual is the crux of all Sabbat Ritae. To join the Sword of Caine, a vampire must participate in the Vaulderie. She may not benefit from any other Ritae until she has participated. The ritual is performed as described in <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>Once performed, each member of the pack has the equivalent of a third stage blood bond to all other members. This ritual shatters any Vinculums the characters already have, though this may constitute a breaking point for blatantly acting against a regnant. Unlike a true blood bond, the Vaulderie only lasts a month and a day, and must be renewed within that time. If the Vaulderie expires, all other Ritae effects are broken. Only a Priest may perform this ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 08-13-2016, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}